### Draft model (`configs/qwen3-8b-dspark-moe-8x1536-top1-2layer-causal-noconf-b16.json`)

| item | setting |
|---|---|
| architecture | DSparkDraftModel, block_size 16, **2 layers** (all full attention), residual hidden 4096, **GQA 8 heads / 2 KV heads**, head_dim 128 (attention width 1024, 1/4 of the 5-layer skeleton), `is_causal: true` (PR #960); same structure as the dense-1/8 arm |
| MoE FFN | per layer 8 routed SwiGLU experts of width 1536 (2 layers, 16 experts in total), top-1 softmax routing without top-k renormalisation (`num_experts_per_tok` 1, `norm_topk_prob` false), no shared expert, router centering `sample` (momentum 0.99), auxiliary balance loss 0.001, `grouped_mm` dispatch, preset `qwen3_5_moe` |
| comparison arm | dense-1/8 (`dense-1/8`, `configs/qwen3-8b-dspark-dense-1-8-2layer-causal-noconf-b16.json`): the same 2-layer, 8/2-head skeleton with one dense MLP of width 1536; this MoE replaces that MLP by 8 x 1536 top-1 experts, so the active MLP width is identical (1536) and the MLP parameters are 8x (12288 = the full dense MLP width) |
| target feature layers | 1, 9, 17, 25, 33 (kept at 5 although the draft has 2 layers; the dspark projector is 5 x 4096 -> 4096) |
| Markov head / confidence head | vanilla, rank 256 / off |
| projector / mask_token_id | dspark / 151669 |
| rope_theta / max_position_embeddings | 1e6 / 40960 |
| vocab | 151936, untied; frozen target embedding (`model.embed_tokens.weight`) |
| size | about 0.49B parameters in total (2 x (attention 10.5M + experts 151M + router) + projector 84M + Markov head and norms 78M), about 0.22B active per token; the dense-1/8 arm is about 0.22B |

