### Deviations from the dense run

- Global batch 132 instead of 128: 128 does not divide over 6 trainer ranks; 2 x 11 x 6 = 132 is the branch's standard for the 2-server + 6-rank layout (the dense-1/8 arm runs 1 x 19 x 7 = 133). A 1-server + 7-rank layout was profiled and rejected: the single capture server ran stop-and-go against the producer window and did not beat two servers.
- 40 epochs: 12 in one run with one cosine schedule, then 4 warm-started continuation run(s); `deployment.managed_local` cannot resume a run, so each continuation starts from the previous run's final checkpoint (draft weights only; fresh AdamW state) and logs into the same W&B run with its steps offset by all earlier steps (`SPECFORGE_LOG_STEP_OFFSET`). (The dense run planned 6 epochs and stopped at step 40,960.)
  - epochs 13-18 (`qwen3-8b-dspark-moe-8expert-1activate-dense-same-cont13to18`): warm start from the epoch-12 checkpoint, re-warmup 4% to 6e-4, cosine to 0, prompt_seed 54, W&B steps offset by 129,173.
  - epochs 19-24 (`qwen3-8b-dspark-moe-8expert-1activate-dense-same-cont19to24`): warm start from the epoch-18 checkpoint, re-warmup 1% to 2e-4, cosine to 0, prompt_seed 60, W&B steps offset by 193,759.
  - epochs 25-32 (`qwen3-8b-dspark-moe-8expert-1activate-dense-same-cont25to32`): warm start from the epoch-24 checkpoint, re-warmup 1% to 2e-4, cosine to 0, prompt_seed 78, W&B steps offset by 258,345.
  - epochs 33-40 (`qwen3-8b-dspark-moe-8expert-1activate-dense-same-cont33to40`): warm start from the epoch-32 checkpoint, re-warmup 1% to 2e-4, cosine to 0, prompt_seed 90, W&B steps offset by 344,460.
- The upstream PR stack #957-#963 is merged (same stack as the dense-1/8 branch) plus #966 (cost-balanced consumer dispatch, a scheduling-only change that keeps each optimizer window's sample membership), so `is_causal: true`, `flatten_vocab_projection`, `cache_vocab_projection`, `ddp_bucket_cap_mb: 128`, one DDP gradient sync per window and the system-prompt removal apply exactly as in the reference run.
- Structure shrunk like the dense-1/8 arm: 2 layers instead of 5 and GQA 8/2 heads instead of 32/8; the dense FFN is replaced by 8 x 1536 top-1 experts (no shared expert); every other draft-config field is the dense skeleton.

