## How the numbers are computed

- Metrics come from the trainer console log (`step N: {...}`, one line every `log_interval` = 10 optimizer steps, rank-deduplicated); the same values are on W&B under `train/*`.
- Epoch k covers optimizer steps ((k-1) x 10,764, k x 10,764]; the last epoch runs to total_steps. The producer keeps 1,420,903 of the 1,420,909 rows (6 have fewer than 2 trainable tokens), so one epoch is 1,420,903 / 132 = 10,764.42 optimizer steps and total_steps = 129,173; the k x 10,764 windows end at most 5 steps before the true epoch boundaries.
- *epoch mean* averages all logged points in the window; *end of epoch* averages the last 20 logged points (200 optimizer steps, about 26k samples).
- *wall-clock* is the time between consecutive epoch checkpoints (epoch 1: since launch); it includes the dataset cache build for epoch 1.
- Exports are `specforge export --to hf` of the epoch checkpoint with the frozen Qwen3-8B embedding, plus the Qwen3-8B tokenizer; the raw training checkpoints (optimizer state included) stay on the box under `/scratch/ckpt-keep/`.

